<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Amcoal raises half yr shr, div.</title>
<headline>Amcoal raises half yr shr, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended Sept 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)	   1,680.4 vs 1,283.6</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			 420.0 vs   300.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income		   434.1 vs   323.4</p>
<p>    Pre-tax			   668.8 vs   510.8</p>
<p>Tax</p>
<p>    - current			 213.8 vs   157.0</p>
<p>    - deferred			 20.9 vs    22.9</p>
<p>    - secondary tax on cos	  -   vs     7.4</p>
<p>    Interest/Investment income  137.7 vs    88.7</p>
<p>    Turnover			1,620.9 vs 1,380.7</p>
<p>Div payable on register November 22</p>
<p>Full name: Anglo American Coal Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was offering capitlsiation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast half-year earnings per share of 1,658.3, with the range between 1,575 and 1,700, and a dividend of 400 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
